"Press the key marked A, and the letter a appears on the screen. It seems to happen at once, and it seems simple. It is not simple. Between your finger and the screen, that key press changes form four times. Let us follow it. Under each key there is a switch. When you press the key, the switch closes, and the keyboard sends the computer a number. The number does not mean a letter. It means a key: it says which key was pressed. On a USB keyboard, the A key is key number 4. The keyboard sends the same number whether you are holding Shift or not, and it reports again when you let the key go. Now the computer has to decide what the key means. It looks at three things: the key number, whether Shift is down, and the keyboard layout you have chosen. From these it picks a character. Key 4 with no Shift gives a. Key 4 with Shift gives A. As you saw in Lesson 2, every character has its own number: a is 97, and A is 65. The number 97 is stored in memory as eight bits: 01100001. The program you are typing in now has a new character to work with, and the processor carries out that program’s instructions, one small step at a time, just as in Lesson 6. If you save your work, the bits are copied to storage, as in Lesson 7. You still cannot see anything. To show the character, the computer needs a shape for it, and the shapes come from a font. A font is a collection of shapes for characters. The computer uses the font to decide which pixels on the screen to light, and the letter appears. Choose a different font and other pixels light up, but the character in memory is still 97. This is the pattern of every computer: input, processing, output. An input device, such as a keyboard, a mouse, or a microphone, turns something from the outside world into electrical signals in binary code. The computer works on them. An output device, such as a screen, a printer, or a speaker, turns the signals back into something a person can understand. Switches, bits, codes, a processor, memory: everything in the first eight lessons took part in that one key press.": "7ad8bddb689d",
